# Files that must stay byte-exact on every checkout (Checkpoint 7b load test, finding 5). With core.autocrlf=true (Git for
# Windows' default) a fresh checkout wrote every tracked fixture and the app icon with CRLF, and 5 tests failed: the
# DynastyProcess CSV fixture, which the tests pad with LF rows (csv-parse reads every record by the first line's ending),
# and src/app/icon.svg, which scripts/make-icons.ts writes byte for byte. "-text": no end-of-line conversion either way
# (safe for binary files too, unlike eol=lf), so a checkout holds exactly what's committed (LF).
fixtures/** -text
src/app/icon.svg -text
